message: >-
  If you use or discuss the SPO-SI research framework, please cite this
  repository and its specific version. A DOI will be added after registration.
type: software
title: 'Subject–Predicate–Object Structural Intelligence (SPO-SI): Subject-Centric World Models, Governed Action, and Recursive Structural Evolution'
authors:
  - family-names: Tan
    given-names: Sizhe
  - name: GPT-Obot
    affiliation: AI research collaborator
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-10-19'
url: 'https://github.com/sizhet/Subject-Predicate-Object-Structural-Intelligence'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/sizhet/Subject-Predicate-Object-Structural-Intelligence'
abstract: >-
  SPO-SI is an open research incubator proposing subject–predicate–object
  intelligence loops, subject-centric and shared world models, structural
  relay contracts, perspective transformations, evidence and counter-evidence
  exchange, and governed recursive structural evolution. Its initial release
  presents conceptual architecture, directional hypotheses, and validation
  plans; it does not claim experimental validation.
keywords:
  - structural intelligence
  - subject-predicate-object
  - subject-centric world models
  - shared world models
  - structural relay
  - perspective transformation
  - counter-evidence
  - governed recursive self-improvement
  - collective learning
  - open research
